1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,563
第一部分，我们建好了索引：分块、向量化、加载
In part 1, we built the index: chunk, embed, load.

2
00:00:03,883 --> 00:00:05,483
第二部分让它派上用场
Part 2 puts it to work.

3
00:00:05,803 --> 00:00:09,685
不过先测试一下：合上笔记本，索引还在吗？
But first, a test: does the index survive closing the laptop?

4
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,746
怎么离开，README 里没写
Leaving isn't in the README.

5
00:00:12,066 --> 00:00:17,165
输入 exit，再在笔记本上列出所有 container：docker ps -a
Type exit, and on the laptop, list every container with docker ps -a.

6
00:00:17,485 --> 00:00:20,820
CLI container 已经没了，退出时就被删掉了
The CLI container is gone, removed on exit,

7
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,931
但 Chroma 还在运行，port 8000 也还被占着
but Chroma is still up, and port 8000 is still taken.

8
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:28,836
要停掉它，在 repo 目录里运行：docker compose down
To stop it, run docker compose down from the repo folder.

9
00:00:29,156 --> 00:00:31,610
有两条警告，说这两个变量没有设置
Two warnings say the variables aren't set.

10
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:34,449
它们无害：只有脚本会设置这两个变量
They're harmless: only the script sets them,

11
00:00:34,449 --> 00:00:36,452
而 down 这条命令两个都不需要
and the down command needs neither.

12
00:00:36,772 --> 00:00:39,119
然后 Chroma 和网络就删掉了
Then Chroma and the network are removed.

13
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:40,967
现在什么都没在运行了
Nothing is running now.

14
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,977
但你磁盘上的 docker-volumes 目录里
But the docker-volumes/ folder on your disk

15
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:47,424
数据库文件和两个索引目录都还在
still holds the database file and both index folders,

16
00:00:47,424 --> 00:00:50,481
outputs 目录里的 chunk 文件也原封未动
and your chunk files in outputs/ are untouched.

17
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:54,429
改天回来，再跑一次：sh docker-shell.sh
Back another day: sh docker-shell.sh again.

18
00:00:54,749 --> 00:00:57,309
不 pull，也不构建：image 已经有了
No pull, no build: the image exists.

19
00:00:57,629 --> 00:01:02,136
要是 git pull 改了依赖或 Dockerfile
After a git pull that changes the dependencies or the Dockerfile,

20
00:01:02,136 --> 00:01:04,285
先运行：docker compose build
run docker compose build first.

21
00:01:04,605 --> 00:01:06,205
暂停一下，重新启动
Pause and restart.

22
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:14,373
两个额外检查：两个 collection 都回来了，维度都是 256
Two extra checks: both collections are back, with dimension 256,

23
00:01:14,373 --> 00:01:19,458
一条叫 --get 的额外命令，返回的还是那 10 条记录的 ID
and an extra command called --get returns the same 10 record IDs.

24
00:01:19,778 --> 00:01:23,233
那个 container 是一次性的；数据从来不住在它里面
The container was disposable; the data never lived in it.

25
00:01:24,583 --> 00:01:26,183
现在看下面那条通道
Now the bottom lane.

26
00:01:26,311 --> 00:01:29,444
问题经过同一个 embedding 模型
The question goes through the same embedding model

27
00:01:29,444 --> 00:01:33,202
变成一个查询向量，和那些 chunk 在同一个空间里
and becomes a query vector, in the same space as the chunks.

28
00:01:33,522 --> 00:01:35,996
查询就是找它的最近邻
Querying means finding its nearest neighbors.

29
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:39,390
课上拿查询给每个存好的向量打分
The lecture scores every stored vector against the query.

30
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:46,260
0.57、0.77、0.43、0.93
0.57, 0.77, 0.43, 0.93.

31
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:50,462
按分数排序，保留 top K，K 是事先定好的
Sort by score, and keep the top K, with K fixed in advance.

32
00:01:50,782 --> 00:01:52,382
这份代码用的是 10
This code uses 10.

33
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:56,866
有一点不同：课上按相似度排名，越高越好
One difference: the lecture ranks by similarity, where higher is better.

34
00:01:57,186 --> 00:02:02,669
Chroma 报的是余弦距离，也就是 1 减去相似度，越小越近
Chroma reports cosine distance, one minus the similarity, where smaller is closer.

35
00:02:02,989 --> 00:02:05,122
顺序一样，方向相反
Same order, opposite direction.

36
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:07,420
而且一次查询总会返回 K 个结果
And a query returns K results

37
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,891
只要有 K 个 chunk 可用，不管相关不相关
whenever K chunks are available, relevant or not.

38
00:02:11,211 --> 00:02:13,964
这份代码里没有任何地方设置距离阈值
Nothing in this code sets a distance threshold.

39
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,323
代码里，query 函数先设定问题
In the code, the query function sets the question,

40
00:02:17,323 --> 00:02:20,445
用同一个 Google 模型把它变成向量
turns it into a vector with the same Google model,

41
00:02:20,445 --> 00:02:22,818
再打开这个 chunk type 的 collection
and opens the chunk type's collection.

42
00:02:23,066 --> 00:02:28,378
第 1 步：python cli.py --query，用 char-split
Step 1: python cli.py --query --chunk_type char-split.

43
00:02:28,698 --> 00:02:31,266
先说一个小疏漏：它打印的是 load 这个词
A small slip first: it prints load(),

44
00:02:31,266 --> 00:02:33,626
这个标签是从加载的代码里抄过来的
a label copied from the load code.

45
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:35,526
然后它连上了 Chroma
Then it connects to Chroma,

46
00:02:35,526 --> 00:02:39,621
但在把问题向量化时卡在了密钥上，还没开始搜索
but stops at the key while embedding the question, before it searches.

47
00:02:39,866 --> 00:02:44,282
问题必须先变成向量，数据库才能拿它来比较
The question must become a vector before the database can compare it,

48
00:02:44,282 --> 00:02:48,058
而只有同一个 Google 模型才能做出同一个空间里的向量
and only the same Google model makes one in the same space.

49
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,732
第 2 步用 recursive-split 再跑一次
Step 2 runs it on recursive-split.

50
00:02:51,052 --> 00:02:56,705
有密钥的话，要找的是：256 个 embedding 值、查询，以及结果
With your key, look for 256 embedding values, the query, and the results.

51
00:02:57,025 --> 00:03:00,622
结果是列表套列表：每个查询一个列表
The results are lists of lists: one list per query,

52
00:03:00,622 --> 00:03:03,937
里面装着 ID、距离、元数据和文档
holding IDs, distances, metadata and documents.

53
00:03:04,257 --> 00:03:05,857
暂停一下，两条都跑一遍
Pause and run both.

54
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:11,256
所以后面 chat 这一步读的是 documents 的第 0 项
That's why chat, later, reads documents[0].

55
00:03:11,576 --> 00:03:15,992
我们没有录到任何结果，所以接下来直接去问加载好的数据库
No results were recorded, so next we ask the loaded database directly.

56
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:20,981
代码发出的查询是这样的：10 个结果，加两个过滤条件
Here's the query the code sends: 10 results and two filters.

57
00:03:21,301 --> 00:03:25,184
元数据过滤只留一本书：The Complete Book of Cheese
The metadata filter keeps one book, The Complete Book of Cheese.

58
00:03:25,504 --> 00:03:28,789
文档过滤留下包含 Italian 的 chunk
The document filter keeps chunks that contain Italian.

59
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:30,996
问题问的是 Tolminc
The question is about Tolminc.

60
00:03:31,316 --> 00:03:33,236
那 10 个结果会讲什么？
What will the 10 results be about?

61
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:45,176
额外检查一下：在加载好的 collection 里数一数
An extra check counts them in the loaded collection.

62
00:03:45,496 --> 00:03:51,854
在 8248 个 chunk 里，按书过滤留下 1355 个
Of 8,248 chunks, the book filter keeps 1,355.

63
00:03:52,174 --> 00:03:54,302
再按 Italian 这个词过滤，留下 64 个
The word Italian keeps 64.

64
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,120
有多少提到 Tolminc？
How many mention Tolminc?

65
00:03:56,419 --> 00:03:58,471
一个都没有。现在来搜索
None. Now a search.

66
00:03:58,791 --> 00:04:02,021
真正的问题要靠 Google 才能变成向量
The real question needs Google to become a vector,

67
00:04:02,021 --> 00:04:05,831
所以我们用一个替身：故事里一个 chunk 存好的向量
so we use a stand-in: the stored vector of one story chunk.

68
00:04:06,151 --> 00:04:10,644
不加过滤，它最近的 10 个全都来自这个故事
Without filters, its 10 nearest are all from the story,

69
00:04:10,644 --> 00:04:14,727
距离从 0，也就是这个 chunk 自己，到 0.16
at distances from 0, the chunk itself, up to 0.16.

70
00:04:14,966 --> 00:04:16,376
加上代码里的过滤
With the code's filters,

71
00:04:16,376 --> 00:04:19,489
10 个结果全都来自 The Complete Book of Cheese
all 10 results come from The Complete Book of Cheese.

72
00:04:19,809 --> 00:04:24,310
它们的距离在 0.28 到 0.31 之间
Their distances run from 0.28 to 0.31.

73
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,156
过滤先起作用
The filters act first,

74
00:04:26,156 --> 00:04:30,732
top K 再用剩下的东西填满 10 个位置，不管有多远
and top K fills its 10 places with whatever survives, however far.

75
00:04:30,966 --> 00:04:34,215
课上把元数据过滤放在排序之后
The lecture puts metadata filtering after ranking:

76
00:04:34,215 --> 00:04:38,177
放在这里，故事的 10 个 chunk 就会全部被丢掉，什么也不返回
here, that would drop all 10 story chunks and return nothing.

77
00:04:38,497 --> 00:04:42,422
Chroma 先过滤，所以你会拿到 10 个结果，讲的却是别的奶酪
Chroma filters first, so you get 10 results, about the wrong cheese.

78
00:04:42,666 --> 00:04:48,421
一个小疏漏：README 说有各种过滤，但只有第 4 种会运行
A small slip: the README promises various filters, but only variant 4 runs;

79
00:04:48,421 --> 00:04:51,029
第 1 到 3 种都被注释掉了
variants 1 to 3 are commented out.

80
00:04:51,349 --> 00:04:55,274
把第 1 种取消注释：不加过滤，每个 chunk 都来竞争
Uncomment the first, with no filter, and every chunk competes.

81
00:04:55,594 --> 00:04:59,072
还有，$contains 是关键词过滤，不是关键词排序
And $contains is a keyword filter, not a keyword ranking.

82
00:04:59,316 --> 00:05:01,928
重启后检查用的那条 --get 命令
The --get command from the restart check

83
00:05:01,928 --> 00:05:05,844
用了同样的按书过滤，但没有问题，所以也没有距离
uses the same book filter, but no question, so no distances.

84
00:05:06,164 --> 00:05:09,085
这 10 条记录，最前面是 Gutenberg 的开头声明
Its 10 records start with the Gutenberg header,

85
00:05:09,085 --> 00:05:11,135
接着是书名页和书的目录
then the title page and contents.

86
00:05:11,455 --> 00:05:14,229
这段声明，还有每本书结尾的许可证
That header, and each book's closing license,

87
00:05:14,229 --> 00:05:17,556
都会像普通文本一样被建进索引：先把它们去掉，再分块
are indexed like any text: strip them before chunking.

88
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,450
接下来是生成
Now generation.

89
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:26,315
课上最终的 prompt 有三部分
The lecture's final prompt has three parts:

90
00:05:26,315 --> 00:05:30,112
规定模型行为的 system prompt、用户的查询
a system prompt that says how to behave, the user's query,

91
00:05:30,112 --> 00:05:32,993
以及从数据库检索到的上下文
and the context retrieved from the database.

92
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:35,375
到了 chat 这一步，代码再查询一次
In chat, the code queries again,

93
00:05:35,375 --> 00:05:38,119
这次不加过滤，要 10 个结果
this time with no filter, for 10 results.

94
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:40,595
然后它拼出 input prompt
Then it builds the input prompt:

95
00:05:40,595 --> 00:05:44,490
先是问题，后面跟着 10 个 chunk，用换行符连起来
the question, followed by the 10 chunks, joined by newlines.

96
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:47,946
这个 prompt 发给 gemini-3.1-flash-lite
The prompt goes to gemini-3.1-flash-lite.

97
00:05:48,183 --> 00:05:49,847
那 system prompt 在哪儿？
So where's the system prompt?

98
00:05:50,167 --> 00:05:53,337
第 40 行定义了一个：只根据 chunk 回答
Line 40 defines one: answer only from the chunks,

99
00:05:53,337 --> 00:05:56,055
chunk 里的信息不够时就直说
and say so when they don't contain enough.

100
00:05:56,375 --> 00:05:57,818
可是看看这次调用
But look at the call.

101
00:05:57,868 --> 00:05:59,217
它从来没被发出去
It's never sent.

102
00:05:59,267 --> 00:06:03,576
一个小疏漏，改一行就能修好：通过一个 config 参数把它传进去
A small slip, with a one-line fix: pass it in a config argument.

103
00:06:03,896 --> 00:06:06,094
更早的 pipenv 分支确实把它发出去了
The older pipenv branch did send it.

104
00:06:06,414 --> 00:06:11,363
没有它，README 承诺的有依据的回答就只能靠这些 chunk 了
Without it, the README's promise of grounded answers rests on the chunks alone.

105
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:14,565
再注意一下什么没变：模型本身
And notice what didn't change: the model itself.

106
00:06:14,885 --> 00:06:16,435
权重一个都没动
No weights moved.

107
00:06:16,485 --> 00:06:19,237
把 collection 删掉，这些知识就没了
Delete the collection, and the knowledge is gone.

108
00:06:19,483 --> 00:06:22,760
第 1 步和第 2 步：python cli.py --chat
Steps 1 and 2: python cli.py --chat,

109
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:26,310
分别用 char-split 和 recursive-split
for char-split and for recursive-split.

110
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:29,446
没有密钥，两条都停在把问题向量化这一步
Without a key, both stop embedding the question.

111
00:06:29,766 --> 00:06:33,734
每个问题要一次 embedding 调用，加一次 Gemini 调用
Each question costs one embedding call and one Gemini call.

112
00:06:33,983 --> 00:06:38,942
有密钥的话，要找的是查询，它打印出来带两个问号
With your key, look for the query, printed with two question marks,

113
00:06:38,942 --> 00:06:42,346
一个无害的小疏漏，还有它的 256 个 embedding 值
a harmless slip, and its 256 embedding values.

114
00:06:42,666 --> 00:06:45,495
然后是结果、数字 10、input prompt
Then the results, the number 10, the input prompt

115
00:06:45,495 --> 00:06:47,978
里面有你的 chunk，以及模型的回答
with your chunks, and the model's response.

116
00:06:49,217 --> 00:06:50,924
还记得开头那个问题吗？
Remember the opening question?

117
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,546
这个故事是虚构的
The story is fiction,

118
00:06:52,546 --> 00:06:57,110
所以回答里讲到 Mara、她祖父和凝乳的内容，来自你的 chunk
so an answer about Mara, her grandfather and the curd came from your chunks.

119
00:06:57,430 --> 00:07:01,078
关于 Tolminc 的现实规定，来自模型的记忆
Real-world rules for Tolminc came from the model's memory.

120
00:07:01,398 --> 00:07:03,020
比较两种 chunk type 的结果
Compare both chunk types.

121
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,613
第 3 步是一个链接，指向课程的对话工具，用 Chrome 打开
Step 3 is a link to the course's chat tool, in Chrome.

122
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:08,933
暂停一下
Pause:

123
00:07:08,933 --> 00:07:11,816
用你的密钥，把两条 chat 命令都跑一遍，再试试这个工具
run both chat commands with your key, then try the tool.

124
00:07:12,136 --> 00:07:17,405
想问你自己的问题，就改 cli.py 的第 372 行
For your own question, change line 372 of cli.py.

125
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:25,443
回到分块，看看课上最好的答案：在意思变化的地方切开
Back to chunking, with the lecture's best answer: cut where the meaning changes.

126
00:07:25,763 --> 00:07:29,371
在课件上，一个锚点沿着这些句子一路往前走
On the slides, an anchor walks through the sentences

127
00:07:29,371 --> 00:07:33,465
把相邻的句子并进来，前提是相似度保持在 0.8 以上
and joins neighbors while their similarity stays above 0.8.

128
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:36,943
代码用的是同样的材料，规则却不一样
The code uses the same ingredients with a different rule.

129
00:07:37,263 --> 00:07:41,611
每个句子都有一个窗口：它自己，加上两边各一个相邻的句子
Every sentence gets a window, itself and one neighbor on each side,

130
00:07:41,611 --> 00:07:43,428
每个窗口都要向量化
and each window is embedded.

131
00:07:43,667 --> 00:07:47,320
然后它量出每个窗口和下一个窗口之间的距离
Then it measures the distance between each window and the next,

132
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,045
画在文本上方，就像地震仪一样
and plots it over the text, like a seismograph.

133
00:07:50,283 --> 00:07:55,680
接着它在第 95 百分位画一条线，在每个超过这条线的尖峰处切开
Next, it draws a line at the 95th percentile, and cuts at every spike above it.

134
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,371
所以最大的那 5% 的落差，就成了 chunk 边界
So the biggest 5 percent of gaps become chunk boundaries.

135
00:07:59,617 --> 00:08:02,384
用 char-split 时，chunk 这一步没有密钥也跑通了
char-split ran the chunk step without a key.

136
00:08:02,476 --> 00:08:04,076
那 semantic-split 行吗？
Can semantic-split?

137
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:18,417
不行。要找出意思在哪里转折，它得先把每个句子窗口都向量化
No. To find where the meaning shifts, it has to embed every sentence window first.

138
00:08:18,737 --> 00:08:21,606
看看交给分块器的那个函数
Look at the function handed to the chunker:

139
00:08:21,606 --> 00:08:25,543
generate text embeddings，和 embed 这一步用的是同一个
generate_text_embeddings, the same one the embed step uses.

140
00:08:25,783 --> 00:08:30,391
README 里的命令，用 semantic-split 把三步一起跑
The README's command runs all three steps with --chunk_type semantic-split.

141
00:08:30,711 --> 00:08:33,574
在我们的机器上，它在 chunk 这一步里就失败了
On our machine it fails inside the chunk step,

142
00:08:33,574 --> 00:08:36,685
卡在第一本书，一个 chunk 都还没保存
on the first book, before a single chunk is saved.

143
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:39,199
有密钥的话，先做好预算
With your key, budget for it:

144
00:08:39,199 --> 00:08:44,121
按我们的估算，给语料分块大约要 528 次 embedding 调用
by our estimate, about 528 embedding calls to chunk the corpus,

145
00:08:44,121 --> 00:08:48,496
向量化这些 chunk 还要大约 90 次，再加 10 到 20 分钟
about 90 more to embed the chunks, and 10 to 20 minutes.

146
00:08:48,816 --> 00:08:52,357
先只放一本书试试，再把其他的放回去，重新跑一遍
Try one book first, then put the others back and run it again.

147
00:08:52,677 --> 00:08:54,573
要找的是每本书的 chunk 数
Look for a chunk count per book,

148
00:08:54,573 --> 00:08:58,544
最后是插入 semantic-split-collection 完成的那一行
and finally, finished inserting into the semantic-split-collection.

149
00:08:58,783 --> 00:09:00,899
切出来的 chunk 长短很不均匀
The chunks come out very uneven,

150
00:09:00,899 --> 00:09:04,735
就连只讲一个主题的书，也会在它最大的几处落差上被切开
and even a single-topic book gets cut at its biggest gaps.

151
00:09:05,055 --> 00:09:08,042
之后再加一个额外步骤：chat 这一步也一样能用
Afterwards, an extra: chat works the same way.

152
00:09:08,362 --> 00:09:10,175
暂停一下，用你的密钥试试
Pause and try it, with your key.

153
00:09:13,517 --> 00:09:15,117
课上走得更远
The lecture goes further.

154
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:19,533
它的框架加了一个检索前阶段和一个检索后阶段
Its frame adds a pre-retrieval stage and a post-retrieval stage.

155
00:09:19,853 --> 00:09:25,592
语义分块属于检索前：这是这个教程唯一实现了的进阶手段
Semantic chunking sits in pre-retrieval: the one advanced lever this tutorial implements.

156
00:09:25,912 --> 00:09:28,344
下面再讲三个，只讲思路
Here are three more, as ideas only.

157
00:09:28,584 --> 00:09:31,379
同样在检索之前：查询改写
Also before retrieval: query rewriting.

158
00:09:31,699 --> 00:09:36,627
用一个模型把杂乱的问题改写成干净的问题，比如“海豚住在哪里”
A model turns a cluttered question into a clean one, like where do dolphins live.

159
00:09:36,947 --> 00:09:40,616
但要是给它一个含糊的问题，改写可能会编造细节
But hand it a vague question, and the rewrite can invent details.

160
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:43,969
检索阶段：混合检索
In retrieval: hybrid search.

161
00:09:44,289 --> 00:09:48,108
关键词能锁定名字和罕见词；向量能抓住意思
Keywords pin down names and rare words; vectors catch meaning.

162
00:09:48,428 --> 00:09:49,828
拿这个问题来说
Take the question:

163
00:09:49,828 --> 00:09:52,605
Chester went to the bank of the river in the morning
Chester went to the bank of the river in the morning.

164
00:09:52,673 --> 00:09:55,020
两种方法给三个段落排出的顺序不一样
The two rank three paragraphs differently.

165
00:09:55,267 --> 00:10:00,029
倒数排名融合给每个段落记二分之一除以它的排名
Reciprocal rank fusion gives each paragraph one half divided by its rank,

166
00:10:00,029 --> 00:10:02,051
每个列表各记一次，再加起来
in each list, and adds them up.

167
00:10:02,371 --> 00:10:09,539
和问题几乎同义的那一段以 0.75 胜出，领先 0.67 和 0.42
The near paraphrase wins with 0.75, ahead of 0.67 and 0.42.

168
00:10:11,034 --> 00:10:13,125
检索之后：重排序
After retrieval: re-ranking.

169
00:10:13,445 --> 00:10:17,985
一个快速的检索器，向量在问题出现之前就做好了
A fast retriever, whose vectors were made before the question existed,

170
00:10:17,985 --> 00:10:21,359
它返回 25 个候选，对的那几个散落在其中
returns 25 candidates with the right ones scattered.

171
00:10:21,679 --> 00:10:25,988
再由一个更慢的模型，把问题和每个 chunk 放在一起读，重新排序
A slower model reads each question and chunk together and reorders them.

172
00:10:27,284 --> 00:10:29,673
这些都不在 cli.py 里
None of these is in cli.py.

173
00:10:29,993 --> 00:10:34,804
你会用上它们，是在朴素检索取回了错的 chunk 的时候
They're what you reach for when naive retrieval brings back the wrong chunks;

174
00:10:34,804 --> 00:10:37,929
而我们那个带过滤的查询，只需要把过滤去掉
our filtered query only needed its filter removed.

175
00:10:40,767 --> 00:10:42,367
该拆掉了
Time to tear down.

176
00:10:42,431 --> 00:10:46,168
输入 exit，再在 repo 目录里运行：docker compose down
Type exit, then docker compose down from the repo folder:

177
00:10:46,168 --> 00:10:50,431
还是那些无害的警告，然后 Chroma 和网络就没了
the same harmless warnings, then Chroma and the network are gone.

178
00:10:52,350 --> 00:10:53,850
这些 image 还在
The images stay:

179
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:59,088
CLI 的 image 有 2.11 GB，包括它的 Python base image
2.11 gigabytes for the CLI image, its Python base included,

180
00:10:59,088 --> 00:11:01,694
Chroma 的有 826 MB
and 826 megabytes for Chroma.

181
00:11:01,934 --> 00:11:06,201
现在 git status 只显示你对 docker-shell.sh 的改动
Now git status shows only your edit to docker-shell.sh.

182
00:11:06,521 --> 00:11:09,641
而 outputs 和 docker-volumes 两个目录都被忽略
The outputs/ and docker-volumes/ folders are ignored,

183
00:11:09,641 --> 00:11:11,134
留在你的磁盘上
and stay on your disk.

184
00:11:11,184 --> 00:11:13,488
Google Cloud 上没有任何东西一直在运行
Nothing keeps running in Google Cloud;

185
00:11:13,488 --> 00:11:15,429
你只为发送过的内容付了费
you paid only for what you sent.

186
00:11:15,749 --> 00:11:17,579
把密钥放在 repo 旁边
Keep the key beside the repo:

187
00:11:17,579 --> 00:11:21,872
放在里面的话，git 不会忽略它，image 也会把它复制进去
inside it, git wouldn't ignore the key, and the image would copy it.

188
00:11:22,192 --> 00:11:23,792
课程结束后，把它删掉
Delete it when the course ends.

189
00:11:24,112 --> 00:11:28,122
先暂停，再把它拆掉，这样下次 port 8000 就是空着的
Pause, then tear down, so port 8000 is free next time.

190
00:11:30,367 --> 00:11:34,975
最后一个教训，来自课程团队留下的下节课 agent 的运行记录
One last lesson, from the staff's recorded run of next lecture's agent.

191
00:11:35,295 --> 00:11:37,528
它检索到的是讲转场放牧的文本
It retrieved text about transhumance

192
00:11:37,528 --> 00:11:40,692
来自一本更早的 Tolminc 书，当天就被换掉了
from an older Tolminc book, replaced that same day.

193
00:11:41,012 --> 00:11:46,068
数据库只根据加载进去的内容回答：书一变，就要重建索引
The database answers from what was loaded: when the books change, rebuild the index.

194
00:11:46,317 --> 00:11:49,197
下节课会用一个 agent 来跑这条命令
Next lecture runs this command with an agent.

195
00:11:49,517 --> 00:11:53,336
在课程团队的那次运行里，模型自己选了要调用哪个检索工具
In the staff's run, the model chose which retrieval tool to call.

196
00:11:53,656 --> 00:11:55,860
课上讲的 Self-RAG 走得更远
The lecture's Self-RAG goes further:

197
00:11:55,860 --> 00:12:00,269
由模型决定到底要不要检索，然后再检查它找到的东西
the model decides whether to retrieve at all, then checks what it found.

198
00:12:00,589 --> 00:12:04,194
我们的 chat 每个问题都要翻书，而且什么都不检查
Our chat opens the book for every question, and checks nothing.

199
00:12:05,434 --> 00:12:07,034
那四个问题呢？
And the four questions?

200
00:12:07,162 --> 00:12:09,594
所谓 embedding，就是表示意思的一个方向
An embedding is a direction for meaning.

201
00:12:09,914 --> 00:12:13,626
向量数据库存的是记录，再用一个索引来搜索它们
A vector database stores records, with an index to search them.

202
00:12:13,946 --> 00:12:16,698
查询找的是问题的最近邻
A query finds the question's nearest neighbors.

203
00:12:17,018 --> 00:12:20,196
上下文，就是你贴进 prompt 里的那些 chunk
The context is the chunks you paste into the prompt.

204
00:12:20,434 --> 00:12:22,439
五道题，自测一下
Five questions to test yourself.

205
00:12:22,759 --> 00:12:26,941
第一题：哪些参数属于哪条通道，两条通道又必须共用什么？
One: which flags belong to each lane, and what must both lanes share?

206
00:12:27,261 --> 00:12:31,195
第二题：为什么 CLI 按名字就能找到数据库
Two: why does the CLI reach the database by name,

207
00:12:31,195 --> 00:12:33,042
又是谁在用 port 8000？
and who uses port 8000?

208
00:12:33,284 --> 00:12:35,609
第三题：重叠有什么好处，又有什么代价？
Three: what does overlap buy and cost?

209
00:12:35,929 --> 00:12:38,895
还有，为什么递归切分器切出了更多 chunk？
And why did the recursive splitter make more chunks?

210
00:12:39,215 --> 00:12:42,863
第四题：README 里的查询为什么没返回任何 Tolminc 文本？
Four: why did the README's query return no Tolminc text?

211
00:12:43,183 --> 00:12:46,297
第五题：这个 prompt 少了什么，又该怎么修？
Five: what is the prompt missing, and what's the fix?

212
00:12:46,534 --> 00:12:51,717
答案在练习里，每条命令都在学习指南里
The answers are in the exercises, and every command is in the study guide,

213
00:12:51,717 --> 00:12:53,617
就在 MLOps Learning 这个 repo 里
in the MLOps Learning repo.

214
00:12:53,937 --> 00:12:55,558
下节课：agent
Next time: agents.
